\f31506\fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
how is the floppy pen when you wiggle it loosely in between your fingers and a toy bow with a suction cup with a string thats not wound tight and the grip of the pen by the hand related
\par 09:31
\par These three phenomena are related through }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 standing wave mechanics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 , }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 node/antinode physics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 , and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 rotational pivots}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 .
\par Here is exactly how these three specific examples connect:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 1. The Floppy Pen Illusion
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls1\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid556457 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 The Action:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
 You pinch a rigid pen loosely at about one-third of its length and waggle your hand up and down.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 The Physics:}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457  Your fingers act as a loose, flexible pivot point (a }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 node}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
 of minimal displacement). The ends of the pen whip back and forth dynamically (the }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 antinodes}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
). Because the human eye cannot process the rapid changes in direction at the tips, your brain smooths out the motion. This creates the optical illusion that the rigid plastic is bending like rubber. [}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 HYPERLINK "https://www.penguinmagic.com/p/S5188"}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 {\*\datafield }}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
