\jclisttab\tx720\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls19\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid556457 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 The Sensory Filter:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
 When your photoreceptors (specifically the rods and cones in your peripheral vision) receive the exact same unchanging light levels for too long, they stop firing signals to your brain. [}{\field\fldedit{\*\fldinst {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/UofGlasgow/posts/for-our-next-trick-the-fading-picture-keep-your-gaze-focused-on-the-black-cross-/2017975904888781/"}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
{\*\datafield }}}{\fldrslt {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \cs35\ul\cf23\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 1}}}\sectd \ltrsect\linex0\endnhere\sectlinegrid360\sectdefaultcl\sftnbj {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 ]
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 The Background Noise Rule:}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
 Your brain treats unmoving peripheral data exactly like the feeling of the clothes on your body or the smell of your own house. It classifies it as "useless background static" and simply stops processing it to save energy.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \f3\fs20\kerning2\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 \loch\af3\dbch\af31506\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid556457\charrsid556457 The Peripheral Weakness:}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457  
Because your peripheral vision has a very low density of receptors compared to the center of your eye (the fovea), it is incredibly easy for your brain to "override" the edges of your vision and fill them in with whatever color is dominant in the center.

\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid556457 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid556457\charrsid556457 
