\par The Troxler effect is a visual illusion where objects in your peripheral vision slowly disappear when you stare at a fixed point. When the eyes stay still, the brain begins to ignore unchanging information, causing colors, shapes, or patterns around the f
ocus point to fade away. Nothing on the screen changes your brain filters it out. Why it happens: Your brain is optimized for change. When there\rquote s no movement, it stops paying attention. Try it: Stare at the center dot for 20\endash 
30 seconds without moving your eyes. #TroxlerEffect #OpticalIllusion #VisualPerception #BrainScience #Neuroscience MindTricks
